  "worked_solution": "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 1)+2(2\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 1)+(2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-22+20+4 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|2|=2.\n$$",
